Random hacking hints:

To run emacs-cl's own test suite:
  make check
or, from inside lisp/:
  bash test
or, from a running session:
  (load "tests.lisp")

The ansi-test/ directory (a checkout of the public ANSI Common Lisp
conformance suite) is the longer-term target test suite; see its own
README for how it's organized. It is not yet wired up to run under
emacs-cl.

Loading load-cl.el (or any other file) twice may well not work.
Individual functions can usually be redefined (with M-C-x or similar),
but to reload the whole system, restart Emacs and load load-cl.el.

To see the Emacs Lisp code generated by the compiler:
  (el:|compile2| (... Common Lisp code ...))
